{
  "id": 204608150,
  "iid": 9763,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Sharkd: Add column header labels to the \"status\" output",
  "description": "Sharkd can be started up with a specific analysis profile, but there is\nno other way of displaying the column header _names_. Displaying frame\ndata only returns the values of each column.\n\nSimilarly, the \"info\" command returns the list of column \"shortcodes\"\nbut not the actual header name string saved in the profile.\n\nThis patch adds the current column header names to the output of the\n`status` command, as it is a good indication that the file is loaded and\nready for decoding.\n\n\n### Example\n\nLaunch `sharkd` reading and writing to STDOUT:\n\n```bash\nrun/sharkd -\n```\n\n```json\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"status\"}\n{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"result\":{\"frames\":0,\"duration\":0.000000000,\"columns\":[\"No.\",\"Time\",\"Source\",\"Destination\",\"Protocol\",\"Length\",\"Info\"]}}\n```\n\n\n### Changes since initial MR:\n\n- change logic to only show columns if `file.cinfo.num_cols > 0`.\n- updated tests cases for sharkd output",
  "state": "merged",
