      "title": "Sharkd: Add column header labels to status command",
      "message": "Sharkd: Add column header labels to status command\n\nSharkd can be started up with a specific analysis profile, but there is\nno other way of displaying the column header _names_. Displaing frame\ndata only returns the values for each column.\n\nSimilarly, the \"info\" command returns the list of column \"shortcodes\"\nbut not the actual header text saved in the profile.\n\nThis patch adds the current column header names to the output of the\n\"status\" command, as it is a good indication that the file is loaded and\nready for decoding.\n\nUpdates `test/suite_sharkd.py` with the new expected output.\n",
